# Testing Conventions

Vitest + React Testing Library are configured and in use. Run with `bun run test`
(`bun test` invokes Bun's own runner and will not work).

## Layout

Tests are **colocated** next to what they cover, named `Component.test.tsx`, and import
the unit directly rather than through the barrel:

```tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';
import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';

import Details from './Details';
```

`vitest.config.mts` collects `{app,components,config,lib,hooks}/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}`.
Two settings there are load-bearing:

- **`globals: true`** — Testing Library registers its between-test DOM cleanup only when
  `afterEach` exists as a global. Without it, cleanup silently stops.
- **`server-only` is aliased to `test/stubs/`** because Vitest does not set the
  react-server condition. The guard still holds in the real build.

`vitest-setup.ts` polyfills `PointerEvent` (Motion's press gesture constructs them) and
forces `prefers-reduced-motion`, and stubs pointer capture, which Radix reaches for on
any press and jsdom does not implement. jsdom needs the Node floor `.nvmrc` sets.

## The jsdom constraint that shapes most tests here

**jsdom gives every element a zero-sized box.** Motion's layout projection therefore
never settles, so a subtree animating out through a shared `layoutId` never unmounts and
an exit animation never completes.

Assert the *state*, not the disappearance:

```tsx
// Good: the trigger's ARIA state is deterministic.
expect(trigger).toHaveAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');

// Bad under jsdom: this subtree may never unmount.
await waitFor(() => expect(screen.queryByText('Nested content')).not.toBeInTheDocument());
```

Where a morph and a dialog are split across two components, assert dismissal on the one
that owns the dialog, not the one that owns the morph. Animation fidelity belongs in a
real browser, not here.

CSS-driven output is invisible too: jsdom does not render `content: counter(...)`, so
assert the marker hook exists rather than the glyph.

## Principles

- Prefer accessible queries (`getByRole`) over `getByTestId`.
- Test what the user sees and does, not internals.
- Server Components: test the utilities they call (`lib/post-utils.ts`,
  `lib/image-utils.ts`) directly; stub the client island when testing what the server
  hands over.
- `vi.restoreAllMocks` only undoes `vi.spyOn`. Reset globals you stub yourself.
- When an assertion looks strange, leave one line saying why. Those comments are the
  point; see the writing-style rule in [CLAUDE.md](/CLAUDE.md).
